            description: "a promising, early-fall apple for Indiana, ripens about a month ahead of Jonathan and has good fruit quality. The tree is upright, rather willowy in growth, hardy, productive, very susceptible to fire blight, and tends to be biennial in bearing if not properly thinned. The fruit, which stores well, is uniform and medium-sized with a shape similar to McIntosh. It has good red color overlying a greenish ground color"
