            description: "is a vigorous, spreading, productive tree that tends toward biennial production unless well thinned. It is a McIntosh-type apple with a slightly coarser fruit texture. The fruit is firmer, more highly colored, and develops an attractive overall oxblood color in central Indiana. The flesh is creamy white and of excellent flavor and quality. The fruit size is medium to large. It stores well into midwinter. Empire is suggested where a high quality, McIntosh-type apple is desired"
